 "aria_snapshot": "- banner:\n  - text: Lumen Upload a spreadsheet. Know what to do next.\n  - button \"Use another file\"\n- main:\n  - complementary:\n    - heading \"What matters most\" [level=3]\n    - paragraph: The average monthly amount in the most recent 8 months is 43% higher than in the first 8. Across product, a single value (Hoodie) accounts for 75% of total amount. You depend heavily on it.\n    - heading \"Findings\" [level=3]\n    - text: amount is up 43% over the period\n    - paragraph: The average monthly amount in the most recent 8 months is 43% higher than in the first 8.\n    - text: Hoodie drives 75% of amount\n    - paragraph: Across product, a single value (Hoodie) accounts for 75% of total amount. You depend heavily on it.\n    - text: amount moves with unit_price\n    - paragraph: amount and unit_price are strongly positively related (correlation 0.83). This shows they move together, not that one causes the other.\n    - heading \"What to do next\" [level=3]\n    - list:\n      - listitem: Find out what changed and repeat it.\n      - listitem: Protect what makes Hoodie work, and test whether other product values can grow.\n      - listitem: Track unit_price alongside amount and test changing it.\n    - heading \"Your data\" [level=3]\n    - paragraph: \"9,046 rows, 6 columns. Main measure: amount.\"\n  - text: Rows analysed\n  - strong: 9,046\n  - emphasis\n  - text: Total amount\n  - strong: 8.3M\n  - emphasis\n  - text: Latest full month\n  - strong: 622k\n  - emphasis: +16% vs previous month\n  - text: Best month\n  - strong: 622k\n  - emphasis: Dec 2025\n  - heading \"Ask a question\" [level=2]\n  - paragraph: Type it the way you would ask a colleague.\n  - textbox \"Question\":\n    - /placeholder: e.g. Which product sold the most last quarter?\n    - text: bar\n  - button \"Ask\"\n  - button \"Which product brings in the most amount?\"\n  - button \"How did amount change month over month?\"\n  - button \"Which product is growing fastest?\"\n  - alert\n  - text: Answer checked against the data\n  - paragraph: Hoodie leads with 6,195,600 in sales, far ahead of Mug (800,700) and Tote bag (763,500). Sticker pack is the smallest at 112,980.\n  - img: 6.2M 801k 764k 425k 113k Sticker pack Notebook Tote bag Mug Hoodie\n  - img\n  - img\n  - group: How this was worked out\n  - heading \"At a glance\" [level=2]\n  - paragraph: Charts picked automatically from your columns.\n  - paragraph: amount by month\n  - img: Peak 622k Jan 2024 Apr 2024 Jul 2024 Oct 2024 Jan 2025 Apr 2025 Jul 2025 Oct 2025 Jan 2026 0 100k 200k 300k 400k 500k 600k\n  - img\n  - img\n  - paragraph: amount by product\n  - img: 6.2M 801k 764k 425k 113k Sticker pack Notebook Tote bag Mug Hoodie\n  - img\n  - img\n  - paragraph: amount by region\n  - img: 2.9M 2.5M 1.7M 1.2M South North Online Campus\n  - img\n  - img\n  - heading \"Data Preview\" [level=2]\n  - paragraph: View your data before and after automatic cleaning.\n  - button \"Raw Input\"\n  - button \"Cleaned Output\"\n  - table:\n    - rowgroup:\n      - row \"order_date datetime64[us] product str region str quantity int64 unit_price int64 amount int64\":\n        - columnheader \"order_date datetime64[us]\"\n        - columnheader \"product str\"\n        - columnheader \"region str\"\n        - columnheader \"quantity int64\"\n        - columnheader \"unit_price int64\"\n        - columnheader \"amount int64\"\n    - rowgroup:\n      - row \"2024-01-01T00:00:00 Hoodie North 1 900 900\":\n        - cell \"2024-01-01T00:00:00\"\n        - cell \"Hoodie\"\n        - cell \"North\"\n        - cell \"1\"\n        - cell \"900\"\n        - cell ",
